  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Hosts",
      "items": [
        "ModularMonolith.Host composes Catalog, Billing and Ledger, and Inventory too when no broker is configured.",
        "Inventory.Host composes Inventory alone and receives Catalog's ProductCreatedV1, ProductCreatedV2 and ProductSnapshotV1 from RabbitMQ.",
        "A Host keeps its Modules' schemas and its message store in one database: the Host fails when built if a Module's DbContext names another."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Optional neighbours",
      "items": [
        "RabbitMQ only with ConnectionStrings:broker: one durable queue per kind of Host, named by its service name.",
        "Redis only with ConnectionStrings:cache; no Kit package references Redis.",
        "OTLP only through the ServiceDefaults recipes, when OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT is set; PouryaKit.Observability exports nothing, and ModularMonolith.Host composes no exporter.",
        "A model provider for Catalog's agent: Ollama's OpenAI-compatible API at localhost:11434 in the sample's settings, or OpenAI or Azure OpenAI through the same client; the provider's HTTP client keeps the Host's resilience pipeline.",
        "An S3-compatible store for the report Module's files: a local RustFS at localhost:9000 in the sample's settings, or AWS S3 through the same provider."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust",
      "items": [
        "Every endpoint is authenticated by default.",
        "The Host does not start unless its bearer scheme validates the issuer, audience, signature and lifetime, from configured values or the Authority.",
        "A trusted peer is named by its authenticated Actor claim, never by a header; outgoing calls carry the Kit's Operation Context headers, never the bearer token."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Reverse proxy",
      "items": [
        "ModularMonolith.ReverseProxy forwards each request by route to a Host that service discovery resolves, the bearer token and the Kit's headers as the client sent them; it runs no Operation. YARP still sets Host and X-Forwarded-*.",
        "The trace id arrives unchanged, and the proxy's span is the parent of the Host's request.",
        "It probes each Host's /alive; the sample's settings turn that off for ModularMonolith.Host, which composes no service defaults."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
